    "df"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "e6e171c0-d811-4346-8fa7-a937d8250f25",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "If you want to view the cleaned and simplified words, also known as the tokens, use the code below. I commented out \"docs_list\" code because that will show every token in 1 column."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 62,
   "id": "8b4cd7ee-8f38-4c4e-9177-05792caa5ef0",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "docs_list = list(df.tokens)\n",
    "#docs_list"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "5665795e-e093-4191-996b-bbbf440280ac",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Part 3: Apply the Method "
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "5ca41cee-39a0-4239-941f-f545fef8a5e7",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Now let's build a dictionary that maps each unique token to a unique ID"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 41,
   "id": "269e0503-1832-4379-8cac-c44ccc95e4ab",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "text/plain": [
       "<gensim.corpora.dictionary.Dictionary at 0x223e0d5dc90>"
      ]
     },
     "execution_count": 41,
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "execute_result"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "gensim_dictionary = Dictionary(df.tokens)\n",
    "gensim_dictionary"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "99342345-9f97-434f-ab47-8d64b43f0388",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Now we will filter out words that are too rare or too common so that the model can give us more coherent topics.\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "Then we recreate our corpus using this cleaner dictionary. \n",
    "\n",
    "KEY DECISION: If we want to limit our token dictionary, we can use the code below to remove words ones that are too common or too rare.\n",
    "\n",
    "For example:\n",
    "\n",
    "no_below=2 means keep words that appear in at least 2 documents\n",
    "no_above=0.3 means remove words that appear in 30% or more of documents.\n",
    "\n",
    "Changing these numbers lets you control how strict the filtering is. To be more specific, increasing \"no_below\" removes more rare words, while decreasing \"no_above\" removes more common words. You can always play around with these numbers, but let's start with \"2\" and \"0.6\""
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 64,
   "id": "1916d291-3ffd-45a0-b667-40aa63444394",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "gensim_dictionary.filter_extremes(no_below=2, no_above=0.6)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "0af78614-bb51-401a-bfeb-2bac87448f0c",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "We print the length of the corpus at the end to make sure we still have 11 (for the 11 movies)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 67,
   "id": "6df46efd-30bf-45a7-a1bd-ec752085802b",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "11\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "corpus = [] #initialize with an empty list\n",
    "for doc in docs_list:\n",
    "    corpus.append(gensim_dictionary.doc2bow(doc))\n",
    "print(len(corpus))\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "51b191d4-4d4c-4d17-a5f8-cd0a0d9c27a0",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Now comes the fun part of running the model! \n",
    "\n",
    "KEY DECISION: Start small with the number of topics, but you can change it to anything you want."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 77,
   "id": "e463da86-250d-4752-a2f6-3139c7b2597d",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "NUM_TOPICS = 4 # the number of topics to extract, you can change this to any number\n",
    "RANDOM_STATE = 5643 # for replication\n",
    "\n",
    "gensim_dictionary[0] # required to initialize, ensures dic is loaded before training LDA\n",
    "word_id = gensim_dictionary.id2token #gensim_dictionary.id2token is a mapping from word IDs to words.\n",
    "\n",
    "lda_model = LdaModel(    #running the model\n",
    "    corpus=corpus,\n",
    "    id2word=word_id,\n",
    "    num_topics=NUM_TOPICS,\n",
    "    random_state = RANDOM_STATE,\n",
    ")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "4f5fa303-962a-4a0d-81bd-ca5b6443ebaa",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Part 4: Results and (Ideas for) Validation"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "41884b2c-b949-4731-a1bd-981969762d10",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Let's print out the top 6 words from each topic (this number can be changed)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 79,
   "id": "4f4cbfab-6aea-4122-89bc-fbe1e5539e79",
   "metadata": {},
