   "source": [
    "lda_model.show_topics(num_topics = -1, num_words= 6, formatted = False)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "292a14bf-0ae6-4c8f-975a-cee47a8541de",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "As you can see, it shows us the groupings of the words, but we have to use our expertise in Star Wars to determine what these topics mean. Furthermore, you can go back to the code labeled \"KEY DECISIONS\" to change those values and see how the topics change.\n",
    "\n",
    "To me at least, here's what the 4 topics mean:\n",
    "\n",
    "1.) Episodes I, II, and III storyline of Anakin with some politics involved\n",
    "\n",
    "2.) Characters in Episodes VII, VIII, and IX\n",
    "\n",
    "3.) Fighting between the Rebels and the Resistance\n",
    "\n",
    "4.) Politics and leadership\n",
    "\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "f58277bb-fc42-4c6f-9e99-e825d58dc0d9",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Now here's a cool visualization! \n",
    "\n",
    "This chart shows each topic as a circle. The bigger the circle, the more common the topic.\n",
    "\n",
    "Circles that are far apart represent distinct topics (while closer circles mean more similar topics), and the bar chart on the right shows the top words overall. When you mouse over a certain topic, it changes to the top 30 words for that topic.\n",
    "\n",
    "You can adjust the slider to see the most frequent words (λ = 1) or the most unique ones (λ = 0).  \n",
    "\n",
    "Topics 1 and 3, related to Episodes I - III and fighting between the Rebels and Resistance, are well separated. However, topics 2 and 4, related to characters in the final trilogy and politics/leadership, are overlapping. Perhaps this means that the final trilogy has a large emphasis on politics and leadership."
   ]
  },
